content.text:
Found a critical issue. `MockBanner.tsx` still uses `localStorage` while `client.ts` switched to `sessionStorage`. And all test files still use `localStorage`. Let me compile the final findings.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "frontend/src/components/MockBanner.tsx",
    "line": 9,
    "summary": "MockBanner reads/writes mock-mode flag from localStorage, but client.ts interceptor now reads it from sessionStorage — mock mode detection is broken",
    "failure_scenario": "Client detects offline → sets sessionStorage('use_mock','true') → reloads → MockBanner reads localStorage('use_mock') → finds nothing → banner doesn't show; user clicks 'Exit Mock Mode' in MockBanner → clears localStorage but sessionStorage still has use_mock=true → mock mode persists"
  },
  {
    "file": "frontend/src/__tests__/context/AuthContext.test.tsx",
    "line": 58,
    "summary": "All ~20 test files still use localStorage for auth tokens, but production code migrated to sessionStorage — every auth-dependent test will fail",
    "failure_scenario": "Test calls localStorage.setItem('access_token','stored-token') → AuthContext useEffect reads sessionStorage.getItem('access_token') → null → user is unauthenticated → protected-route tests, admin tests, and all authenticated-state tests fail"
  },
  {
    "file": "frontend/src/pages/admin/ContentModeration.tsx",
    "line": 437,
    "summary": "Report link uses navigate() in-place instead of target='_blank', navigating admin away from the moderation page — inconsistent with posts/comments tabs",
    "failure_scenario": "Admin clicks report target link to view reported content → current tab navigates to /posts/123 → admin loses place in reports queue and any pending state; must navigate back to /admin/content manually"
  },
  {
    "file": "frontend/src/components/CommentSection.tsx",
    "line": 227,
    "summary": "ReplyItem renders recursively with no depth limit; backend also has no nesting cap — deep reply chains risk stack overflow or unusable UI",
    "failure_scenario": "User scripts 200 nested replies → backend stores them → buildCommentTree serializes full chain → ReplyItem recurses 200 levels deep → browser call stack overflow or extremely laggy render"
  }
]
```

**Summary**: 4 findings. Two are confirmed bugs from the localStorage→sessionStorage migration (MockBanner out of sync, all tests broken). One is a regression in my report navigation fix (lost `target="_blank"`). One is a pre-existing risk with unbounded reply nesting.

